\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 I design with intention. Across UX, brand identity, editorial, and print, my work is research-driven, built on the belief that good design asks questions before it answers them.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 My background in scholarly research shaped how I approach design problems. Pratt's MFA program in Communication Design formalized that approach, and it's core to how I work. I don't start with the visual. I start with context: who the audience is, what ideas are actually at stake, and what the work needs to accomplish. The aesthetics follow from that process, not the other way around.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 Right now, I'm looking for full-time graphic design or UX opportunities in New York City, at organizations where communication, people, and culture intersect. I work well independently and in teams, in environments where rigor and curiosity aren't treated as opposites.
\f1\fs24 \

\f0\fs29\fsmilli14667 When I'm not designing, I'm creating art or reading. Drawing, painting, working through a book; the edge between image and language is where I thrive.
\f1\fs24 \
